  "publication_adjustments": [
    "Curated single-package distribution containing @moonglade/provenance 2.6.1.",
    "Aligned with draft-ottley-agentic-epistemic-provenance-03 standard.",
    "Hardened L3 DTA Byzantine median quorum with minimum 3-probe fanout and 3000 ms drift window.",
    "Strict IEEE 754 safe integer enforcement on claims JSON with value-based normalization.",
    "Explicit binary extension mapping including ONNX raw byte fidelity.",
    "Migrated test suite to native Node.js 22/24 test runner (node:test + node:assert/strict), eliminating Jest, Babel, Istanbul, and 314 transitive dev dependencies.",
    "2.6.1 adds the ./self-test export, the B1 binary-mutation regression test and the self-test CLI test; verification behaviour is unchanged from 2.6.0.",
    "2.6.1 includes the WASM core export (wasm/, ./wasm) and the hook installer (provenance install-hooks). The wasm/ files and the ./wasm export shipped in the 2.6.0 npm tarball but were not committed to this repository until public commit 0778caf; the hook installer was not in the 2.6.0 tarball and is first published in 2.6.1.",
    "2.6.1 hardens the hook installer first committed in 0778caf: it refuses to overwrite a foreign hook (--force backs it up), enables only the options the user chooses (flags or per-option prompts), removes the empty pre-push option, and resolves the hooks directory with git rev-parse --git-path hooks. hookInstaller.ts and artifact-cli.ts therefore differ from 0778caf; see hookInstaller.test.js."
  ],
